# Ground side (GSG + MCS + planner + tools [+ rfsim]). Copy to docker/ground.env.
# Also used by the local-demo agent, which must share the session and secret.
# Keys: docs/web_2026-10/LINK_DESIGN.md §4. Never commit the filled-in file.

# Session id and 32-byte hex secret from `python -m smo_link.token new`.
# The space side (docker/space.env) must carry the SAME pair.
SMO_LINK_SESSION=
SMO_LINK_SECRET=
# SMO_LINK_SECRET_FILE=/run/secrets/smo_link_secret

# Host address the MCS (9090), planner (9091), instructor proxy (8080) and
# link (9100) ports are published on. Default 127.0.0.1: none of these ports
# has its own login (the MCS sends TCs), so nothing is reachable from the
# network until you choose. On the GCP VM set the VM's INTERNAL IP, with the
# VPC firewall admitting only the Google LB ranges (130.211.0.0/22,
# 35.191.0.0/16) on these ports and IAP (35.235.240.0/20) on 22 —
# deploy/gcp/README.md §1-2. Never 0.0.0.0 on a public or campus host
# (Docker-published ports bypass ufw). The link port follows the same rule.
# NOTE: compose reads this one for its `ports:` lines, so it takes effect
# ONLY with `docker compose --env-file docker/ground.env ...` (or exported in
# the shell). Without that, the ports stay on 127.0.0.1 whatever you set here.
# On Google Cloud, C2O deploy/gcp/vm-bootstrap.sh writes this file for you.
# SMO_PUBLISH_ADDR=10.20.0.10

# Browser origins allowed through the instructor proxy (comma list). Empty
# means same host only. Set to the public instructor hostname behind the load
# balancer; its host name is then also accepted in the Host header (the proxy
# refuses unknown Host names: DNS-rebinding guard). IP literals and localhost
# are always accepted. Extra Host names: SMO_GSG_ALLOWED_HOSTS (comma list).
# SMO_GSG_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://sim.c2o.live

# Welcome page (portal, 8090). With a domain its links are
# https://<name>.<domain> (ops., plan., sim., tm., ...); without one they are
# http://<host>:<port>. SMO_PORTAL_SIM_HOST: where the instructor tools run
# (default 10.20.0.11, the cloud sim VM, once a domain is set).
# SMO_PORTAL_PROBE (key=host:port list) replaces individual probe targets;
# the compose default probes SpaceCDF and the local-demo instructor tools by
# service name. NOTE: like SMO_PUBLISH_ADDR, SMO_PORTAL_PROBE is read via
# --env-file (it is interpolated into compose.yaml).
# SMO_PORTAL_DOMAIN=c2o.live
# SMO_PORTAL_PROBE=design=spacecdf:8000

# Seconds a TC may wait in the GSG's link queue before it is discarded (and
# reported) instead of sent; the agent applies the same age limit end to end.
# SMO_LINK_TC_TTL_S=5

# MCS upstream: 8002/8001 = the GSG directly; with `--profile rf` use the RF
# bridge instead: SMO_MCS_TM_PORT=8012 and SMO_MCS_TC_PORT=8011.
SMO_MCS_TM_PORT=8002
SMO_MCS_TC_PORT=8001
# RF bridge mode for `--profile rf`: FRAME (CCSDS framing + BER) or RF (BPSK)
SMO_RF_MODE=FRAME

# sim = follow the simulator clock (re-timed by the GSG); real = wall-clock UTC
SMO_TIME_SOURCE=sim

# Optional
# SMO_UI=modern
# SMO_LANG=en

# Voice loops on a laptop: SMO_VOICE=dev makes the MCS mint tokens for the
# compose `livekit` service (profile voice) at ws://<this host>:7880, and lets
# the unverified local user take the instructor roles. On Google Cloud the
# MCS reads docker/voice.env instead (LIVEKIT_URL/API_KEY/API_SECRET, written
# by deploy/gcp/vm-bootstrap.sh). Details: deploy/gcp/README.md "Voice loops".
# SMO_VOICE=dev
